imself  again and he also revealed one of his  greatest strengths as a show of power  the night king lifted his arms and all  of the fallen wildlings opened their  eyes and they started to stand back up  the wildlings eyes were now blue just  like the night kings and the  white walkers I think most of us assume  someone was controlling all of the  whites but when the night King brought  all of the wildlings back to life right  in front of our eyes it pretty much  confirmed it for me  it seems as if the night King is warding  all of the whites at the same time and  there is more evidence of this in later  episodes in season 6 episode 5 we  learned a great deal about the night  King and possibly where he is getting  his powers from while bran was at the  three-eyed Ravens cave he entered the  weirwood net by himself when he did this  he came upon a small force of whites led  by the night king and a few of his white  Walker lieutenants as bran approached  the whites it became obvious that the  whites were motionless almost as if they  were asleep but when he got to the back  of their formation he saw the night King  along with the three white walkers the  night King knew that bran was there and  when he turned his head to look at Bryan  all of the whites had turned around  simultaneously as if they moved when the  night King moved but the night King gave  no commands nor did he motion for them  to move so it seems as if they were all  being controlled by his mind very  similar to warding but the most  important part of this episode was when  we got to see the night King's creation  the night King was created by the  children of the forest after they had  plunged a dragonglass blade into his  chest as the dragonglass pierced his  heart it turned his eyes blue so I think  it's safe to say the night King was the  first white Walker to have blue eyes and  it could help explain why all the other  White Walkers and whites eyes are blue  too because they are all under control  of their master the night king it's very  similar to what happens when we see  Bryan warg into an animal or even Hodor  Bran's eyes roll back in his head and  turn white then the eyes turn white with  whatever he is working into when we saw  the night Kings creation it made perfect  sense why he would have the same type of  powers as well only the night King is  much more powerful than brain as right  now the night King was created by the  chosen of the forest and the children of  the forest get their powers from the old  gods one of their main power sources is  the weirwood trees and in this episode  we learned the night king can tap into  that power source as well which is why  the night king was waiting for bran when  he entered into the weirwood net the  children gave the night king all these  powers when they created him and bran  has these  same powers - he just hasn't learned how  to harness them yet we have seen brand  Morgan to animals and even people just  like the night king but we haven't seen  bran be able to control an entire army  yet but Bryan also has a power that we  haven't seen the night king use yet  either and this is where we get into the  main part of this theory there is one  awesome power that wargs or skinchangers  have not only can they control animals  but they can also live second knives  through these animals if they are about  to die they can't enter the mind of  something else and live on through that  there is a great example of this in this  show during season 3 episode 9 when John  is traveling with the wildlings they  have a ward with them named Orel while  John is with them they order him to kill  this old man to prove that he is one of  them but John refuses to do it in a  fight breaks out during this fight John  manages to shove his sword into orals  chest but he is able to cheat death with  his working abilities and right before  he dies he wargs into the eagle and he  uses the Eagle to attack John John might  have stopped 